version: 1
name: Cliff Bench
half: 60.0
runway: -6.00 -20.00 6.00 -8.00

# CLIFFS - a drop painted as a FACE instead of a ramp.
#   --map worlds/test_cliff.world
#
# The cell is 0.538 m here. A cell carrying `cliff` steps at the line where the bilinear crosses the
# midpoint of its own two tiers, and the mesh cuts the same line, so the floor drawn is the floor walked.
#
#   EAST   a 6.00 m mesa with a straight face at x 12, and a seven-section ladder up it (6.30 m, head
#          0.30 m proud of the lip - inside `env.LADDER_PROUD`).
#   SOUTH  a 4.00 m shelf whose face runs the DIAGONAL x + z = 20, which is the case the lattice cannot
#          hold as a ramp.
#   NORTH  a STAIR flight up the mesa's west face at a 0.90 grade - past MAX_SLOPE 0.839, so it walks only
#          because each tread is flat and each riser is one `wf.STAIR_RISE`.
#   MIDDLE a `stairflight` PROP up the mesa at z -4: the stair that is a deck, not a terrace. And a 1 m POOL
#          dug against the same face at z -0.5..8.5, so that face stands in water: wet stone to
#          `env.FACE_WET_H` over the sheet and a pale tide line to `FACE_TIDE_H` above it.
#   WEST   a 3.00 m pit with a ramp down its west side. The ramp is NOT flagged, so it stays walkable and
#          proves the two live side by side. FLOODED to the plain, so its painted east wall is wholly under
#          the sheet.
#
# Walk off any lip and it is a fall, not a snap (`game.heroFooting`). Nothing on foot will follow you off
# one (`env.brink`).

zone: meadow -400.0 -400.0 400.0 400.0 0.220 grasstall,patch,tuft,clover,moss,wildflowers
clear: 0.0 0.0 26.0

at: bonfire -2 -20 0 1

# The wall it leans on is its local -Z, so yaw 270 puts the open side at world -x: the plain.
at: ladder 12 -16 270 1 rise=6.3

# A FLIGHT up the same face: six 1.0 m sections over 9.6 m of run, walked and not climbed. Local -Z is the
# wall it climbs to, like the ladder, so yaw 270 climbs east from its foot at x 2.4 to the lip at x 12.
at: stairflight 2.4 -4 270 1 rise=6.0


